-- Every action requires a session, meaning an Authorization header must be
-- present. AXL does not validate it — it forwards it to Skyborn, which resolves
-- it to a Grant and applies the real scope and spending-cap checks.
--
-- Nothing here is PUBLIC. A PUBLIC action would be an unauthenticated proxy
-- straight through to a wallet.
--
-- ROLE and OWNER are deliberately unused: they only work behind a gateway
-- started with --trust-identity-headers that overwrites X-AXL-Subject on every
-- request, and a gate that looks real but reads a client-supplied header is
-- worse than no gate at all.

PERMISSION wallet_balance       : AUTH
PERMISSION wallet_transactions  : AUTH
PERMISSION wallet_topup         : AUTH
PERMISSION wallet_transfer      : AUTH
PERMISSION wallet_refund        : AUTH
PERMISSION wallet_payout        : AUTH
PERMISSION messages_send        : AUTH
PERMISSION messages_read        : AUTH
PERMISSION messages_otp_latest  : AUTH
PERMISSION calls_make           : AUTH
PERMISSION calls_status         : AUTH

-- Rate limits are a blast-radius control, not an authorization check. They are
-- tightest on the actions that move money or reach a third party.
RATE_LIMIT wallet_balance       : 60/min
RATE_LIMIT wallet_transactions  : 60/min
RATE_LIMIT wallet_topup         : 10/min
RATE_LIMIT wallet_transfer      : 20/min
RATE_LIMIT wallet_refund        : 10/min
RATE_LIMIT wallet_payout        : 5/min
RATE_LIMIT messages_send        : 30/min
RATE_LIMIT messages_read        : 60/min
RATE_LIMIT messages_otp_latest  : 30/min
RATE_LIMIT calls_make           : 5/min
RATE_LIMIT calls_status         : 60/min

-- Deliberately no CONFIRM on any action.
--
-- AXL's only confirmation gate is `CONFIRM <action> : OTP`, which holds the
-- call until a second request supplies a one-time code. The engine never
-- returns that code in an API response and has no channel of its own to send
-- it, so satisfying the gate means a human reads it somewhere and types it
-- back — which is precisely the involvement Skyborn exists to remove (spec
-- Section 2: no OTP at call time, ever).
--
-- The control that replaces it is stronger and sits in the right place: the
-- spending cap the human set when approving the Grant, enforced server-side in
-- Skyborn on every money-out call, plus the audit log and one-tap revoke
-- (Section 15). A gate here would trade a real limit for a prompt.
